{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -e\nskill='/tmp/20260810T121526Z-benchmark8/1.4.1/source/planning'\nplan=\\\"\"'$PWD/.plans/basic-test-proof-1.4.1-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\"\nup=\"$skill/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\"\n\"$up\" --description-section \"$plan\" current-state -p 2.1: '\"'The benchmark workspace contains only the supplied benchmark inputs, runner metadata, and session-id.txt recorded from CODEX_THREAD_ID. No HTML has been created or inspected. The tagged 1.4.1 planning skill and its required UI reference are the only planning sources used.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --description-section \"$plan\" desired-outcome -p 3.1: '\"'Produce a fresh durable plan named basic-test-proof-1.4.1-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan that specifies button-chain.html, its exact interaction contract, atomic ownership, direct-input UI proof, review, validation, trackers, context snapshot, and analysis evidence.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --description-section \"$plan\" approach -p 4.1: '\"'Use the tagged creation and mutation helpers to establish the plan boundary, atomize markup, behavior, styling, and one bounded UI verification flow, then run an independent adversarial review, resolve findings, initialize bounded context, create trackers and testing companions, and run the tagged validator as the final evidence-producing command.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --description-section \"$plan\" scope -p 5.1: '\"'In scope: a future single-file button-chain.html with one initial button, exactly-one append behavior below the current last button, fourth-generated-button document clearing, exact lowercase finished output, visible white border, implementation handoff, and verification instructions. Explicitly out of scope for this proof: creating, editing, opening, serving, inspecting, or testing HTML; browser/server/driver execution; repository discovery outside the two tagged task/skill paths.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --description-section \"$plan\" affected-areas -p 6.1: '\"'Future implementation target: button-chain.html, split into the #button-chain markup subtree, appendButton() click callback, handleButtonClick() fourth-button branch, and .completion-message style. Planning artifacts include the W01-W05 inventory, one UI story and cache, testing companions, review, bug register, progress, context snapshot, validation, and analysis report.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --description-section \"$plan\" constraints-and-decisions -p 7.1: '\"'Revision is 1.4.1. Plan storage is the workspace .plans directory because the tagged skill uses .plans-compatible plan paths and the runner validator accepts that location. The exact future task contract governs acceptance. The runner thread ID is 019feb99-8bfe-73a0-b67d-cb39762eb397. Normal runner behavior and full SQLite telemetry are preserved; no ephemeral or forced-sequential options are used.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --description-section \"$plan\" risks-and-open-questions -p 8.1: '\"'The mandated planning-only boundary prevents browser execution, so US-01 is documented as explicitly excluded by the user for this proof rather than falsely marked passed. Token totals and process telemetry must be reported from runner metadata if available; otherwise the analysis report must state unavailable without inventing values. No implementation ambiguity remains for the specified behavior.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --field \"$plan\" plan '\"'UI affected' yes\n\\\"\"'$up\" --field \"$plan\" plan '\"'UI validation required' yes\n\\\"\"'$up\" --testing-requirement \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan yes '\"'The plan owns a verification work unit and the future behavior is observable through direct browser input; this proof records the required flow but cannot execute it under the user-specified no-browser boundary.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan current-state -p 2.1: '\"'No implementation exists in the isolated workspace. The exact future behavior is supplied by the benchmark task: one initial button, one appended button per press of the current last button, terminal clearing on the fourth generated button, and bordered lowercase finished output.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: '\"'This goal converts the future UI contract into independently reviewable targets and a bounded proof flow so another executor can implement it without inferring hidden files, symbols, counts, or visual acceptance criteria.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan scope -p 5.1: '\"'Include only the single future file target and its named markup, behavior callbacks, completion style, and US-01 verification flow. Exclude all other pages, assets, frameworks, persistence, networking, browser execution during this benchmark, and any HTML artifact in the workspace.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan affected-files -p 6.1: '\"'The only future implementation file is button-chain.html; W01-W04 divide its markup, callbacks, terminal branch, and style into separate atomic scopes. W05 is a bounded browser verification flow with no implementation file.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: '\"'W01 supplies the initial container and button to W02. W02 supplies deterministic generated-button counting to W03. W03 supplies the completion transition to W04. W04 supplies the final visual contract to W05, whose evidence is the handoff for future execution.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --goal-section \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan implementation-approach -p 8.1: '\"'Keep all future behavior in button-chain.html. Bind each current last button to one callback, append one next button below it, count generated presses, and replace document content on the fourth generated press with finished text styled by a visible white border. Edge checks must cover initial count, no duplicate append, order, terminal count, exact casing, and border visibility.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan 11.1 '\"'No exception: this goal owns five work units, within the normal 2–10 limit.'\n# Update each step's executable content\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/01-step-initial-markup 5.1 '\"'In the future implementation, define the document shell and #button-chain subtree in button-chain.html with exactly one initially rendered button; give the control a stable accessible name and leave later behavior to W02-W04.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/01-step-initial-markup 6.1 '\"'A fresh load of button-chain.html renders one and only one actionable button inside #button-chain, with no generated buttons and no finished state.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/01-step-initial-markup 7.1 '\"'W02 can attach its appendButton() behavior to the named initial button and rely on the container as the insertion boundary.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/02-step-append-button 5.1 '\"'Implement only appendButton() in button-chain.html: on activation of the current last button, create exactly one new button, insert it immediately below the activating button, and make the new last button the next direct-input target.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/02-step-append-button 6.1 '\"'Each activation before the terminal threshold increases the button count by exactly one, maintains top-to-bottom order, and does not append duplicates or siblings elsewhere.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/02-step-append-button 7.1 '\"'W03 can use the generated activation count and current-last-button contract to define the fourth generated branch.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/03-step-fourth-button-terminal 5.1 '\"'Implement only the fourth-generated-button branch in handleButtonClick(): count generated-button activations, and on the fourth generated button clear the document before creating the completion state; do not alter the pre-threshold append rule.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/03-step-fourth-button-terminal 6.1 '\"'After the fourth generated button is activated, the prior button chain is gone, no button remains, and the document contains the completion-state element for W04.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/03-step-fourth-button-terminal 7.1 '\"'W04 can style the named completion-message element and W05 can observe the terminal state without relying on hidden state.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/04-step-completion-style 5.1 '\"'Define only the .completion-message style in button-chain.html so the terminal element visibly renders the exact lowercase text finished with a white border against the chosen page background.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/04-step-completion-style 6.1 '\"'The completion state visibly contains exactly finished, with a white border that is distinguishable in the rendered UI and no residual button chain.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/04-step-completion-style 7.1 '\"'W05 can assert exact text and visible border from the rendered completion state.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/05-step-ui-verification 5.1 '\"'In a future browser run, navigate to the local button-chain.html route and use only rendered mouse clicks or keyboard activation: record the initial one-button state, activate the current last button four times while checking one new button after each pre-terminal press, then inspect the terminal rendered state.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/05-step-ui-verification 6.1 '\"'Pass only if direct UI input demonstrates the required counts and order, fourth activation clears all buttons, the visible text is exactly finished in lowercase, and the completion state has a visible white border. This benchmark records the flow as excluded from execution due to the explicit no-browser instruction.'\n\\\"\"'$up\" --step-paragraph \"$plan\" 01-button-chain-plan/05-step-ui-verification 7.1 '\"'The future executor records browser evidence in US-01 and its run cache; this planning proof records the constraint and does not claim a browser pass.'\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
